From d6ac33b9dcfba9eb7cc3b8f058d69418637bf760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:02:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Timeout to every xUnit [Fact] in the test projects

Gives each plain `[Fact]` an explicit `Timeout` so a runaway test fails instead
of stalling the run. Facts that already carry a deliberate Timeout are left
alone, and the rewrite is a per-line byte substitution, so the CRLF and mixed
CRLF/LF files here keep their exact line endings.

Value: 600000 ms (10 minutes), matching the parent repository.

xUnit v2 starts a test's timeout clock when the test is queued rather than when
it starts running, so the budget has to clear a whole project's wall-clock or a
queued test can trip it while merely waiting for a slot. The slowest project
here runs about a minute, so 600000 ms leaves roughly ten times that.

Facts in test projects referencing xunit 2.9 or newer are deliberately left
untouched unless they are async: 2.9 fails a synchronous test that carries a
Timeout outright ("Tests marked with Timeout are only supported for async
tests"), where 2.5.3 ignores it and xunit.v3 honours it.
